{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trip record carries the driver's own 'arrived' event for this trip, tapped at 13:45:32, so POL-NS-01(a) is satisfied on the platform's own telemetry.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02743"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "payload.events[driver_arrived].at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's trace satisfies the POL-NS-02 arrival test for a STANDARD pickup: 37 of his 73 fixes are qualifying in-radius fixes against the 50 m radius for this zone class, and the first qualifying in-geofence fix falls at 13:45:32 - at, not after, the 'arrived' event timestamp - which is what POL-NS-01(b) requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02743", "EV-TRIP-02743"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's statement that the driver 'parked a bit away' is contradicted by the measured trace: the driver's closest approach to the pickup pin is 41.4 m, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and the record never places him outside that radius during the arrival window. Nothing in the geometry supports a wrong-face or wrong-block reading.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02743", "EV-TRIP-02743"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver then held position inside the geofence for one continuous run of 360 seconds, from 13:45:32 to 13:51:32 - twice the 180 second free waiting period in force for this trip - so POL-NS-01(c) is met, and the POL-NS-06 shortfall computation shows a surplus, not a shortfall, of 180 seconds.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02743", "EV-TRIP-02743"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip ended with no boarding event and was terminated by the driver at 13:51:35 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW - one of the three codes POL-NS-01(d) recognises - which is more than three minutes after the required dwell elapsed at 13:48:32, so limb (d) also holds.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02743"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "payload.cancellation_reason_code",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival marker is not a false marker under POL-NS-05: at the 13:45:32 marker the trace places the driver inside the geofence at 41.4 m from the pin and stationary at 0.0 km/h, so neither the 300 m trigger nor the 15 km/h trigger fires, the waiting clock runs from the marker, and the full free waiting period was genuinely served.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02743", "EV-TRIP-02743"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider. I concede limb (c): the rider's track is present and 66 qualifying fixes sit within 23.6 m of the pin, so the rider was nearby. But limb (a) fails, and all three limbs are required: the rider's only message is 'ok' at 13:47:02, which is not the rider's own position, not an entrance, block, tower or bay identifier, not a request for the driver's position, and not a statement that the vehicle could not be seen. Without limb (a) the clause does not operate, and the driver's message 'here' at 13:45:52 was in any event never answered with any locating information.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02743", "EV-GPS-02743"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.max_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this pickup: EV-ADVIS-02743-01 is MISSING, carries issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0, so no POL-NS-06 limb (i) aggregation of separate in-geofence intervals is available to either side. The driver needs none: his qualifying dwell is a single uninterrupted run that already exceeds the minimum, and no party may assert anything against a MISSING artifact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02743-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "With POL-NS-01 satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee stands as charged - NO_ACTION on the fee, which on this rider-filed dispute leaves the present payment state intact - and POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of that net fee, SGD 3.60, as the fare ledger computes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02743", "EV-TRIP-02743"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-01", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip and compensation cannot be withheld: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below the threshold of 4, and 2 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 123 is 0.016, below the required 0.08. These are the only two profile fields POL-GEN-01 permits for this test, and no other field on the driver profile carries any weight here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02743"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.6,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute is over the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02743 after the driver cancelled at 13:51:35 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. The fee is properly chargeable and the driver is owed SGD 3.60.\n\nWhy the fee stands (POL-NS-01, read from EV-TRIP-02743, EV-GPS-02743 and EV-FARE-02743). All four limbs hold: (a) the trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 13:45:32; (b) the GPS trace places him inside the arrival geofence for this STANDARD pickup — 37 qualifying fixes (accuracy within 25 m) inside the 50 m radius, the first at 13:45:32, which is the 'arrived' timestamp POL-NS-01(b) requires; (c) he then held position inside that radius in one continuous run of 360 seconds, from 13:45:32 to 13:51:32 — double the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec); and (d) the record shows no boarding and a driver termination at 13:51:35 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises, more than three minutes after the required dwell elapsed at 13:48:32. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee.\n\nTo the rider on your points. You are right that the driver stopped a short distance from the pin, and the trace bears you out: his closest approach was 41.4 m. But the policy measures arrival by the arrival radius, and 41.4 m is inside the 50 m STANDARD radius, so POL-NS-03 (wrong-entrance) — which applies only where the driver's stationary fixes are outside the radius — does not apply, and your account that he 'parked a bit away' does not defeat limb (b). Your own rider track is strong (66 qualifying fixes, 16.3–23.6 m from the pin, stationary from 13:42:45 to after the cancellation; POL-NS-04 limb (c) is met), but POL-NS-01 does not make proof of your absence a condition of the fee — limb (d) reads only the reason code and the absence of a boarding event. The clause that protects a rider who is present and trying to coordinate is POL-NS-04, and it needs all three limbs. Limb (a) fails: your only message in the window is 'ok' at 13:47:02, which is an acknowledgement and none of the things limb (a) lists — not your own position, not an entrance, block, tower or bay identifier, not a request for the driver's position, and not a statement that you could not see the vehicle. Limb (b) is met (the driver posted no reply within 120 seconds and made no in-app call) and so is limb (c), but with limb (a) unmet the clause cannot refund the fee. Your point about the missing traffic advisory is taken: EV-ADVIS-02743-01 is MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0, so no aggregation of separate in-geofence intervals under POL-NS-06(i) is available to either side — but nothing turns on it, because the driver's 360-second run already exceeds the 180-second minimum on its own and there is no shortfall to aggregate.\n\nTo the driver on your points. POL-NS-05 does not fire: at 13:45:32 the trace places you 41.4 m from the pin and stationary at 0 km/h, so neither the 300 m trigger nor the 15 km/h trigger fires, your marker is not false, and no false-arrival referral is recorded. Your statement that you were 'right at the pin' is not exactly what the trace shows, but the geofence test is what governs and it is satisfied. POL-NS-07 then fixes your payout at 80 percent of the net fee in force: 80% x SGD 4.50 = SGD 3.60, the figure the fare ledger computes (EV-FARE-02743). The anti-farming check does not trip — driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2/123 = 0.016 (below 0.08) — so compensation is paid.\n\nOutcome, confidence and execution. The rider's charge of SGD 4.50 stands unchanged (the fee disposition is NO_ACTION), and because compensation is payable the emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, with amount_sgd carrying the same SGD 3.60 as driver_compensation_sgd (POL-GEN-03). Every artifact carrying the deciding facts — EV-TRIP-02743, EV-GPS-02743 and EV-FARE-02743 — is at weight 1.0, so no discount applies under POL-GEN-02 and the MISSING advisory carried no deciding fact. Confidence 0.90, above the 0.70 floor; no ground under POL-NS-09 applies, so there is no escalation. The monetary effect (SGD 3.60) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically under POL-GEN-05. This is a provisional ruling made without human review and either party may appeal it under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.6,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee stands and the driver is paid SGD 3.60.\n\nTHE CHARGE (POL-NS-01). The fee is chargeable only if all four limbs hold, and they do. (a) EV-TRIP-02743 carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 13:45:32. (b) EV-GPS-02743 shows 37 qualifying in-radius fixes for a STANDARD pickup, and the first in-geofence fix falls at 13:45:32 - at, not after, the marker - with the closest approach 41.4 m, inside the 50 m radius. (c) The driver then held one continuous in-geofence run of 360 seconds, from 13:45:32 to 13:51:32, twice the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (EV-TRIP-02743.platform_policy.free_wait_sec). (d) No boarding event is recorded and the trip was terminated by the driver at 13:51:35 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises, more than three minutes after the required dwell elapsed at 13:48:32. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06, and no limb of POL-NS-10, displaces this.\n\nTHE RIDER'S ARGUMENTS. Your account that the driver 'parked a bit away' does not hold against the measurements: POL-NS-02 fixes the arrival radius at 50 m for a STANDARD zone (EV-TRIP-02743.pickup_zone_class) and the driver's own trace never leaves it, so POL-NS-03 - which applies only where the stationary fixes lie OUTSIDE the radius but within 400 m - is not engaged. The same measurement defeats the argument that the fee's premise fails: POL-NS-01 turns on the driver's arrival and dwell, not on where you stood. Your presence at the pin (66 qualifying fixes, furthest 23.6 m, mean 20.0 m, nearest 16.3 m) is real and I accept it, but rider presence is limb (c) of POL-NS-04, not a condition of POL-NS-01. Your route to exoneration under POL-NS-04 requires all three limbs and limb (a) fails: your only message, 'ok' at 13:47:02, is not your own position, an entrance, block, tower or bay identifier, a request for the driver's position, or a statement that you could not see the vehicle - it is a bare acknowledgement, and the clause's enumerated categories do not reach it. Limb (b) (no reply within 120 seconds, in_app_calls empty) and limb (c) (presence) are met, but all three are required, so POL-NS-04 does not operate. POL-NS-06 shows no shortfall - 360 seconds of dwell against a 180-second minimum - and the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02743-01 is MISSING with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight 0.0; both sides cite it only for its absence, limb (i) is unavailable, and it decides nothing here.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S ARGUMENTS. The arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05: at 13:45:32 the trace places you 41.4 m from the pin, under the 300 m trigger, and stationary at 0.0 km/h, under the 15 km/h trigger, so the waiting clock runs from the marker and the full free waiting period was served. POL-NS-07 fixes your payout at 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 net fee, SGD 3.60, as EV-FARE-02743 computes, and the anti-farming check does not trip: EV-DPROF-02743.no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2 divided by 123 completed trips is 0.016 (below 0.08). These are the only two driver-profile fields POL-GEN-01 permits for this test; no other profile field carried weight, and no rider-profile field was used against the rider.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND EXECUTION. Every artifact carrying the deciding facts - EV-TRIP-02743, EV-GPS-02743 and EV-FARE-02743 - is at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and the ruling sits well above the 0.70 escalation floor; neither POL-NS-09 nor POL-GEN-07 is engaged. No clause produces a referral: there was no false arrival marker (POL-NS-05(ii)), no pin-ambiguity goodwill (POL-NS-03(ii)), and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming branch did not fire. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically, subject to the appeal route in POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
